      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ROYAL TORONADO (2) was well fancied when resuming but found one better, a rival here in TOO DARDY, in the Listed Farnley Stakes at this track. Laid the platform for a good campaign ahead and has won second-up three times, so he's right in this. SEARCHIN' TIMES (8) scored by a head last time out over 1400m at this track, which atoned for some luckless efforts. Has a very good record here including three wins from five starts and looks sure to be there at the business end.  TOO DARDY (1) is in a rich vein of form, making it three on end when he accounted for some rivals here and while he jumps in the weights he's going far too well to discount. CORRECT CHOICE (4) resumed over 1400m and turned in a fair run to finish sixth in the Farnley Stakes. Appears suited by the extra journey this time and is expected to run well. ARCADIA PARK (3) resumes here and while he'll be better over further, he is a recent trial winner so might pull out a run fresh.",
